    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling output today, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.07) and **Yordan Alvarez** (71.77). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a top priority despite hitting 8th; his high projection is buoyed by a favorable matchup against Sproat and favorable wind conditions that favor his speed profile, a critical asset given our focus on stealing bases. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Rojas (5.83 xERA), providing the ideal power-category anchor. **Trea Turner** (71.38) continues to provide elite stability out of the leadoff spot, with wind assistance against Lodolo further elevating his efficiency rating into the high-70s tier.\n\nOur platoon-heavy approach has paid dividends in today\u2019s selection, particularly for **Colt Keith** (68.01) and **Carson Benge** (67.24), both of whom capitalize on excellent platoon advantages and top-of-the-order usage. **Casey Schmitt** (62.58) is a calculated risk; assuming he holds his spot in the #3 hole, his dynamic platoon advantage against Gallen creates a surprising value play. Conversely, we must monitor **Hyeseong Kim** (47.43) and **Luke Raley** (48.61), as both are skating the edge of our efficiency floor. **Chase Meidroth** (37.14) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting lineup, but his inability to clear the 40-point benchmark against the stingy Bryan Woo made him the clear choice for the bench. \n\nRisks are concentrated in our mid-tier hitters facing high-skill arms. **Christian Yelich** (54.29) is facing the formidable Imanaga, and his score is depressed by the elite hold capabilities of the opposing staff, which significantly limits his stolen base potential. Similarly, while **Dillon Dingler** (48.56) and **Junior Caminero** (56.55) are in the lineup, both face moderate SP challenges that cap their upside. We remain wary of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Casey Schmitt**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Luke Raley**; any late-scratch or order-tinkering could drop these players below our required performance floor, necessitating a quick evaluation of our bench depth should those lineups officially shift against us.",
